 safety a priority in healthcare settings.<\\\\\\/span><\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ol>\\\"}\"}', '{\"en\":\"{\\\"en\\\":\\\"<ol><li><span style=\\\\\\\"color:hsl(0,0%,30%);font-family:Poppins;font-size:17px;\\\\\\\">Implement effective infection control practices.&nbsp;<\\\\\\/span><\\\\\\/li><li><span style=\\\\\\\"color:hsl(0,0%,30%);font-family:Poppins;font-size:17px;\\\\\\\">Identify and prevent potential safety risks.&nbsp;<\\\\\\/span><\\\\\\/li><li><span style=\\\\\\\"color:hsl(0,0%,30%);font-family:Poppins;font-size:17px;\\\\\\\">Properly use personal protective equipment (PPE) in various healthcare settings.&nbsp;<\\\\\\/span><\\\\\\/li><li><span style=\\\\\\\"color:hsl(0,0%,30%);font-family:Poppins;font-size:17px;\\\\\\\">Understand and apply Standard Precautions&nbsp;<\\\\\\/span><\\\\\\/li><li><span style=\\\\\\\"color:hsl(0,0%,30%);font-family:Poppins;font-size:17px;\\\\\\\">Educate others on safety and infection control protocols.<\\\\\\/span><\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ol>\\\"}\"}', 1, NULL, 0, 1, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 5, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL),
(9, 5, 17, 0, '100', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 9717, 19, '{\"en\":\"Intro to programming\"}', 'intro-to-programming', '1117', '', 'public/uploads/main/images/20-09-2025/68cea0c6cc06b.jpeg', 'public/uploads/main/images/20-09-2025/course-17583720381588349932.png', 0.00, NULL, 0.00, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, '', '', '', '{\"en\":\"<p><strong>Course Description<\\/strong>:<br>This course provides a comprehensive introduction to the fundamental concepts of programming and computational thinking. Designed for beginners, it equips students with the essential skills to write, test, and debug simple programs using a high-level programming language. Topics include variables, data types, control structures (conditionals and loops), functions, basic data structures, and an introduction to object-oriented programming. Through hands-on exercises and projects, students will develop problem-solving skills and gain confidence in writing code to solve real-world proble&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}', NULL, 4, 16000.00, 4.00, 1, '2025-09-20 09:40:38', '2025-12-03 05:03:12', 0, '0', '{\"en\":\"<h3><strong>Course Requirements:<\\/strong><\\/h3><p>To succeed in this course, students are expected to meet the following requirements:<\\/p><h4><strong>1. Technical Requirements:<\\/strong><\\/h4><ul><li>A laptop or desktop computer (Windows, macOS, or Linux) capable of running a code editor or IDE (e.g., VS Code, PyCharm).<\\/li><li>Stable internet connection (for accessing course materials, online coding environments, and submitting assignments).<\\/li><li>Installed programming environment as specified by the instructor (e.g., Python 3.x, Java, or browser-based platforms like Replit).<\\/li><\\/ul><h4><strong>2. Academic Requirements:<\\/strong><\\/h4><ul><li><strong>Basic Computer Literacy<\\/strong>: Familiarity with using a computer, navigating files and folders, installing software, and using a web browser.<\\/li><li><strong>Mathematical Foundation<\\/strong>: Basic knowledge of arithmetic and logical thinking; no advanced math required.<\\/li><\\/ul><h4><strong>3. Course Participation:<\\/strong><\\/h4><ul><li>Regular attendance (for in-person or live online courses).<\\/li><li>Active participation in lectures, discussions, and coding exercises.<\\/li><li>Completion of weekly assignments and lab exercises.<\\/li><\\/ul><h4><strong>5. Time Commitment:<\\/strong><\\/h4><ul><li>Expect to dedicate <strong>6\\u201310 hours per week<\\/strong>, including lectures, readings, assignments, and project work.<\\/li><\\/ul>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p><strong>Learning Outcomes<\\/strong>:<br>By the end of this course, students will be able to:<\\/p><ul><li>Understand the basic principles of programming and software development.<\\/li><li>Use variables, operators, and control structures effectively.<\\/li><li>Design and implement functions to organize code.<\\/li><li>Apply fundamental data structures like lists and dictionaries.<\\/li><li>Debug and test code to identify and fix errors.<\\/li><li>Develop small programs or projects demonstrating practical programming skills<\\/li><\\/ul>\"}', 1, NULL, 4, 1, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 122, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL),
(10, 5, 17, 1, '100', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 9717, 19, '{\"en\":\"{\\\"en\\\":\\\"Intro to programming\\\"}\"}', 'en-intro-to-programming', NULL, '', 'public/uploads/main/images/20-09-2025/68cea0c6dfb8b.jpeg', 'public/uploads/main/images/20-09-2025/course-17583720381599019787.png', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, '', '', '', '{\"en\":\"{\\\"en\\\":\\\"<p><strong>Course Description<\\\\\\/strong>:<br>This course provides a comprehensive introduction to the fundamental concepts of programming and computational thinking. Designed for beginners, it equips students with the essential skills to write, test, and debug simple programs using a high-level programming language. Topics include variables, data types, control structures (conditionals and loops), functions, basic data structures, and an introduction to object-oriented programming. Through hands-on exercises and projects, students will develop problem-solving skills and gain confidence in writing code to solve real-world proble&nbsp;<\\\\\\/p>\\\"}\"}', NULL, 0, 0.00, 0.00, 4, '2025-09-20 09:40:38', '2025-11-03 06:41:29', NULL, '0', '{\"en\":\"{\\\"en\\\":\\\"<h3><strong>Course Requirements:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h3><p>To succeed in this course, students are expected to meet the following requirements:<\\\\\\/p><h4><strong>1. Technical Requirements:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li>A laptop or desktop computer (Windows, macOS, or Linux) capable of running a code editor or IDE (e.g., VS Code, PyCharm).<\\\\\\/li><li>Stable internet connection (for accessing course materials, online coding environments, and submitting assignments).<\\\\\\/li><li>Installed programming environment as specified by the instructor (e.g., Python 3.x, Java, or browser-based platforms like Replit).<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul><h4><strong>2. Academic Requirements:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li><strong>Basic Computer Literacy<\\\\\\/strong>: Familiarity with using a computer, navigating files and folders, installing software, and using a web browser.<\\\\\\/li><li><strong>Mathematical Foundation<\\\\\\/strong>: Basic knowledge of arithmetic and logical thinking; no advanced math required.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul><h4><strong>3. Course Participation:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li>Regular attendance (for in-person or live online courses).<\\\\\\/li><li>Active participation in lectures, discussions, and coding exercises.<\\\\\\/li><li>Completion of weekly assignments and lab exercises.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul><h4><strong>5. Time Commitment:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li>Expect to dedicate <strong>6\\\\u201310 hours per week<\\\\\\/strong>, including lectures, readings, assignments, and project work.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul>\\\"}\"}', '{\"en\":\"{\\\"en\\\":\\\"<p><strong>Learning Outcomes<\\\\\\/strong>:<br>By the end of this course, students will be able to:<\\\\\\/p><ul><li>Understand the basic principles of programming and software development.<\\\\\\/li><li>Use variables, operators, and control structures effectively.<\\\\\\/li><li>Design and implement functions to organize code.<\\\\\\/li><li>Apply fundamental data structures like lists and dictionaries.<\\\\\\/li><li>Debug and test code to identify and fix errors.<\\\\\\/li><li>Develop small programs or projects demonstrating practical programming skills<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul>\\\"}\"}', 1, NULL, 0, 1, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 9, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL),
