 browser.<\\\\\\/li><li><strong>Mathematical Foundation<\\\\\\/strong>: Basic knowledge of arithmetic and logical thinking; no advanced math required.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul><h4><strong>3. Course Participation:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li>Regular attendance (for in-person or live online courses).<\\\\\\/li><li>Active participation in lectures, discussions, and coding exercises.<\\\\\\/li><li>Completion of weekly assignments and lab exercises.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul><h4><strong>5. Time Commitment:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li>Expect to dedicate <strong>6\\\\u201310 hours per week<\\\\\\/strong>, including lectures, readings, assignments, and project work.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul>\\\"}\"}', '{\"en\":\"{\\\"en\\\":\\\"<p><strong>Learning Outcomes<\\\\\\/strong>:<br>By the end of this course, students will be able to:<\\\\\\/p><ul><li>Understand the basic principles of programming and software development.<\\\\\\/li><li>Use variables, operators, and control structures effectively.<\\\\\\/li><li>Design and implement functions to organize code.<\\\\\\/li><li>Apply fundamental data structures like lists and dictionaries.<\\\\\\/li><li>Debug and test code to identify and fix errors.<\\\\\\/li><li>Develop small programs or projects demonstrating practical programming skills<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul>\\\"}\"}', 1, NULL, 0, 1, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 9, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL),
