owser.<\\\\\\/li><li><strong>Mathematical Foundation<\\\\\\/strong>: Basic knowledge of arithmetic and logical thinking; no advanced math required.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul><h4><strong>3. Course Participation:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li>Regular attendance (for in-person or live online courses).<\\\\\\/li><li>Active participation in lectures, discussions, and coding exercises.<\\\\\\/li><li>Completion of weekly assignments and lab exercises.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul><h4><strong>5. Time Commitment:<\\\\\\/strong><\\\\\\/h4><ul><li>Expect to dedicate <strong>6\\\\u201310 hours per week<\\\\\\/strong>, including lectures, readings, assignments, and project work.<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul>\\\"}\"}', '{\"en\":\"{\\\"en\\\":\\\"<p><strong>Learning Outcomes<\\\\\\/strong>:<br>By the end of this course, students will be able to:<\\\\\\/p><ul><li>Understand the basic principles of programming and software development.<\\\\\\/li><li>Use variables, operators, and control structures effectively.<\\\\\\/li><li>Design and implement functions to organize code.<\\\\\\/li><li>Apply fundamental data structures like lists and dictionaries.<\\\\\\/li><li>Debug and test code to identify and fix errors.<\\\\\\/li><li>Develop small programs or projects demonstrating practical programming skills<\\\\\\/li><\\\\\\/ul>\\\"}\"}', 1, NULL, 0, 1, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 9, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL),
(13, 3, 17, 0, '100', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 9717, 19, '{\"en\":\"Database Systems\"}', 'database-systems', '1118', '', 'public/uploads/main/images/21-09-2025/68cf9b6c6245e.jpeg', 'public/uploads/main/images/21-09-2025/course-1758436204145812157.png', 0.00, NULL, 0.00, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, '', '', '', '{\"en\":\"<p>A <strong>Database System<\\/strong> is software that helps to <strong>store, organize, and manage data<\\/strong> in a structured way so it can be <strong>easily accessed, updated, and secured<\\/strong>.<\\/p><ul><li><strong>Key Topics:<\\/strong><ul><li><strong>Data Models:<\\/strong> how data is represented (tables, objects).<\\/li><li><strong>SQL (Structured Query Language):<\\/strong> used to insert, update, delete, and search data.<\\/li><li><strong>Database Design:<\\/strong> creating tables, relationships, primary &amp; foreign keys.<\\/li><li><strong>Normalization:<\\/strong> reducing redundancy and improving efficiency.<\\/li><li><strong>Transactions:<\\/strong> ensure data consistency (commit, rollback).<\\/li><li><strong>Security:<\\/strong> controlling access with users and permissions.<\\/li><\\/ul><\\/li><li><strong>Examples:<\\/strong> MySQL, Oracle, Microsoft SQL Server, PostgreSQL.<\\/li><\\/ul>\"}', NULL, 4, 14000.00, 13.00, 1, '2025-09-21 03:30:04', '2025-12-02 21:07:54', 0, '0', '{\"en\":\"<p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Basic understanding of <strong>Programming Fundamentals<\\/strong> (variables, loops, functions).<\\/li><li>Knowledge of <strong>Data Structures<\\/strong> (arrays, lists, trees, searching, sorting).<\\/li><li>Some background in <strong>Discrete Mathematics<\\/strong> (sets, relations, functions).<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>Technical Requirements:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>A <strong>DBMS software<\\/strong> (MySQL, Oracle, PostgreSQL, or SQL Server).<\\/li><li>A <strong>programming environment<\\/strong> (e.g., Java\\/Python\\/PHP if database connectivity is required).<\\/li><li>Computer with enough storage and memory to run database tools.<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>Skills Needed:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Problem-solving and logical thinking.<\\/li><li>Ability to design models (ER diagrams, schemas).<\\/li><li>Understanding of data organization and file handling.<\\/li><\\/ul>\"}', '{\"en\":\"<p>After completing this course, students will be able to:<\\/p><ol><li><strong>Understand basic concepts<\\/strong> of databases, data models, and architectures.<\\/li><li><strong>Design relational databases<\\/strong> using ER (Entity-Relationship) diagrams.<\\/li><li><strong>Apply normalization techniques<\\/strong> to improve database efficiency.<\\/li><li><strong>Use SQL<\\/strong> for data definition, manipulation, and querying.<\\/li><li><strong>Develop database applications<\\/strong> for real-world problems.<\\/li><li><strong>Implement transaction management<\\/strong> (commit, rollback) for data integrity.<\\/li><li><strong>Apply security measures<\\/strong> like user roles and permissions.<\\/li><li><strong>Work with DBMS software<\\/strong> such as MySQL, Oracle, or SQL Server.<\\/li><\\/ol>\"}', 1, NULL, 13, 1, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 110, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 7, NULL, NULL),
