INSERT INTO `question_banks` (`id`, `type`, `question`, `marks`, `trueFalse`, `suitable_words`, `number_of_option`, `q_group_id`, `category_id`, `sub_category_id`, `active_status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `lms_id`, `user_id`, `image`, `explanation`) VALUES
(11, 'M', 'lol', 1, NULL, NULL, '01', NULL, 17, 0, 1, '2025-08-07 06:46:11', '2025-08-07 06:46:11', 1, 9701, NULL, NULL),
(12, 'M', '<p>dakmldmkda</p>', 4, NULL, NULL, '3', 5, 17, 0, 1, '2025-08-11 02:07:23', '2025-08-11 02:07:23', 1, 1, NULL, '<p>nnnnn</p>'),
(13, 'M', 'Which of the following is considered a vital sign?', 1, NULL, NULL, '4', NULL, 11, 7, 1, '2025-08-21 03:42:03', '2025-08-21 03:42:03', 1, 1, NULL, NULL),
(14, 'M', 'The best way to prevent the spread of infection is:', 1, NULL, NULL, '4', NULL, 11, 7, 1, '2025-08-21 03:43:09', '2025-08-21 03:43:09', 1, 1, NULL, NULL),
(15, 'M', '<p>Which of the following is a high-level programming language?</p>', 10, NULL, NULL, '4', 1, 17, 0, 1, '2025-09-21 07:36:15', '2025-09-21 07:36:15', 1, 1, NULL, '<p>C++ is considered a <strong>high-level programming language</strong> because it allows programmers to write code in a human-friendly way using words and symbols, rather than binary digits or simple mnemonics. Machine language, on the other hand, is just 0s and 1s, which is very hard for humans to understand, while assembly language uses short mnemonics like MOV or ADD that are still tied closely to the hardware. Binary code is simply the raw instructions for the computer. Therefore, among the given options, <strong>C++ is the correct answer</strong> since it is high-level and widely used for application development.</p>'),
(16, 'M', '<p>Which operator is used to compare two values in most programming languages?</p>', 50, NULL, NULL, '4', 1, 17, 0, 1, '2025-09-21 07:38:52', '2025-09-21 07:38:52', 1, 1, NULL, '<p>In most programming languages, the operator == is used to <strong>compare two values</strong> and check if they are equal. The single equals sign = is used only for assignment, meaning it stores a value in a variable rather than checking equality. The plus sign + performs addition, while the logical AND &amp;&amp; checks if two conditions are true. Since the question is about comparison, only == is correct. For example, in C++ or Java, the statement if (x == y) checks whether the value of x is equal to y.</p>'),
(17, 'M', '<p>Which of the following is an advantage of using a DBMS over a traditional file system?</p>', 30, NULL, NULL, '4', 1, 17, 0, 1, '2025-09-21 08:42:19', '2025-09-21 08:42:19', 1, 1, NULL, '<p>One of the main advantages of a DBMS is <strong>centralized control of data</strong>, which helps reduce redundancy, improve consistency, and ensure better security. In file systems, data is stored separately in multiple files, often leading to duplication and inconsistency. A DBMS solves this by managing data in a central way, so option <strong>(c)</strong> is correct</p>'),
(18, 'M', '<p>&nbsp;In the Entity-Relationship (ER) model, a <strong>primary key</strong> is used to:</p>', 40, NULL, NULL, '4', 1, 17, 0, 1, '2025-09-21 08:44:36', '2025-09-21 08:44:36', 1, 1, NULL, '<p>A <strong>primary key</strong> is an attribute (or set of attributes) that uniquely identifies each record in a table. This ensures that no two rows in a table can have the same primary key value. It does not allow duplicates or null values. Therefore, option <strong>(b)</strong> is correct because the primary key’s main role is to uniquely identify each entity.</p>');
